;; spec:   §4, §7 (types §2.10, §6.4, §8.4)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 2
;; audit:  clean
;; The builtin swap! passed as a function value and called through it
;; with a closure. By the closure convention apply2 hands the atom and
;; the closure to swap! with one count each; swap! gives f a count of
;; its own for each call (types §8.6) and releases its owned parameters
;; once. A closure released both by its own body's exit and by the
;; builtin's owned parameter was a release of freed memory (adversary
;; finding 005).
(defun apply2 (f x y) (f x y))
(defun main () -> i64 (let ((a (atom 1))) (apply2 swap! a (fn (x) (+ x 1)))))
